@@ -169,3 +169,16 @@
 ```
 
 Some migration and gateway plugin tests require Bun on PATH and use local plugin fixtures; they skip when Bun is unavailable. Report any skipped tests and verify the community package separately when its implementation changes.
+
+## Native API Key forms
+
+An API auth method may opt into `keyForm: { keysURL, protocols: [{label, value}] }`.
+`methods` in `host.js` validates these display hints and `plugin.Method` carries them
+to the GUI. `renderPluginKeyForm` uses the native Key editor's fields, batch parser
+and menu. Each Key still goes separately through `plugin-signin`, and credentials
+remain in `plugin-auth.json`; no existing account or provider is converted.
+The optional name and protocol go in `inputs.name` and `inputs.protocol`. The plugin
+must validate and explicitly retain them in its authorization metadata, and enforce
+the protocol when listing models and sending requests. A failed batch retains only
+the unprocessed Keys for retry. Older hosts ignore `keyForm` and retain their API
+Key input; plugins must keep that path usable without extra prompts.
